  "id": "DrugBank_DB14488 - MONDO_1239",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Gluconate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Anemia Of Prematurity through a chain of indications that link it to Iron Deficiency Anemia and ultimately to Anemia Of Prematurity. The evidence suggests that Ferrous Gluconate is associated with Microcytic Anemia and Iron Deficiency Anemia, both of which are known to contribute to the development of Anemia Of Prematurity. This suggests a potential mechanism where Ferrous Gluconate may influence iron metabolism, leading to anemia in premature infants. The indirect pathways highlight a possible role of Ferrous Gluconate in the pathophysiology of anemia, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible link, but further research is needed to confirm the direct causal relationship and the role of specific pathways involved.",
